  "i18n": {
    "en": {
      "path": "/en/collection/world-polymer/bangladesh-10-taka-2000/",
      "title": "10 Taka, Bangladesh Bank, Polymer (2000) | Notofilia",
      "description": "Catalog record numismático: banknote de 10 Taka de Bangladesh Bank, primer banknote de polymer de Bangladesh, emitido en el año 2000. Pick P-35.",
      "ogTitle": "Bangladesh Bank — 10 Taka de Polymer (2000)",
      "ogDescription": "Primer banknote de polymer de Bangladesh: 10 Taka de Bangladesh Bank, emitido en el año 2000. Colección privada Notofilia.",
      "template": "<div lang=\"en\" style=\"width:100%; min-height:100vh; background:#0a0a09; font-family:'Cormorant Garamond', serif; box-sizing:border-box;\">\n\n  \n\n  \n\n  <main data-pagefind-meta=\"url:/en/collection/world-polymer/bangladesh-10-taka-2000/\" id=\"main-content\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-screen-label=\"Bangladesh Bank — 10 Taka (2000)\" style=\"max-width:1180px; margin:0 auto; padding:56px 24px 80px; outline:none;\">\n\n    <a href=\"/en/collection/world-polymer/\" style=\"display:inline-block; color:#e7ddc4; text-decoration:none; font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.08em; margin-bottom:24px;\">&larr; World polymer banknote catalog</a>\n\n    <div style=\"background:#d8d2cd; border:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.08); border-radius:3px; padding:clamp(28px,4vw,64px); box-shadow:0 30px 70px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);\">\n\n      <div style=\"display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:center;\">\n\n        <div style=\"text-align:center; max-width:720px; margin:0 auto 40px;\">\n          <span style=\"display:block; font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.22em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; margin-bottom:14px;\">World Polymer Banknotes &middot; Bangladesh &middot; 2000</span>\n\n          <h1 style=\"font-family:'Montenegrin Gothic One', serif; font-weight:400; font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,44px); line-height:1.08; letter-spacing:0.01em; color:#1c1a15; margin:0 0 12px;\">Bangladesh Bank</h1>\n\n          <p style=\"font-size:clamp(19px,2vw,23px); font-style:italic; color:#4a4331; margin:0;\">Ten Taka &middot; Bangladesh's first polymer banknote &middot; Year 2000</p>\n        </div>\n\n        <div style=\"width:100%; max-width:560px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:14px; margin:0 auto 56px;\">\n          <button\n            data-zoom-trigger=\"bangladesh-10-taka-2000-polimero\"\n            aria-label=\"Enlarge image of the banknote\"\n            style=\"all:unset; display:block; width:100%; position:relative; cursor:zoom-in;\"\n          >\n            <picture>\n              <source srcset=\"/uploads/bangladesh-banco-bangladesh-10-taka-2000-polimero.webp\" type=\"image/webp\" />\n              <img\n                src=\"/uploads/bangladesh-banco-bangladesh-10-taka-2000-polimero.jpg\"\n                alt=\"Banknote of Diez Taka de polymer de Bangladesh Bank, obverse arriba con portrait of Sheikh Mujibur Rahman y la mezquita Baitul Mukarram, reverse abajo con el edificio del Parlamento Nacional (Jatiya Sangsad Bhaban)\"\n                width=\"564\"\n                height=\"510\"\n                loading=\"eager\"\n                decoding=\"async\"\n                style=\"display:block; width:100%; height:auto;\"\n              />\n            </picture>\n            <span style=\"position:absolute; bottom:22px; right:22px; display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; background:rgba(10,10,9,0.82); color:#d8d2cd; font-size:13px; letter-spacing:0.08em; padding:8px 14px; border-radius:999px;\">\n              <span style=\"width:6px; height:6px; background:#d8d2cd; transform:rotate(45deg);\"></span>Enlarge</span>\n          </button>\n          <span style=\"font-size:13px; letter-spacing:0.08em; color:#5c4e33; text-align:center; font-style:italic;\">Obverse (top) and reverse (bottom) — Notofilia.com Collection</span>\n<div style=\"display:flex; flex-direction:column;\">\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Country</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Bangladesh</span>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Issuing Entity</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Bangladesh Bank (central bank of the People's Republic of Bangladesh)</span>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Denomination</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Ten Taka (10 Taka)</span>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Material</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Polymer &mdash; Guardian&trade; substrate &mdash; the first polymer banknote issued in Bangladesh</span>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Printer</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Note Printing Australia (NPA), a subsidiary of the Reserve Bank of Australia<sup style=\"font-size:12px;\">4</sup></span>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Year of Issue</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">2000</span>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Signature</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Mohammad Farashuddin, Governor of Bangladesh Bank</span>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Dimensions</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Approximately 123 &times; 60 mm<sup style=\"font-size:12px;\">1</sup></span>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12); border-bottom:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Rarity</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Withdrawn from circulation because of low public acceptance; today it interests collectors as the country's first polymer experiment<sup style=\"font-size:12px;\">2</sup></span>\n            </div>\n            <div style=\"display:grid; grid-template-columns:200px 1fr; gap:6px 20px; padding:14px 0; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12); border-bottom:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n              <span style=\"font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33;\">Catalog Reference</span>\n              <span style=\"font-size:19px; color:#221f19;\">Pick P-35, Standard Catalog of World Paper Money<sup style=\"font-size:12px;\">3</sup></span>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n\n          \n            <div\n              role=\"dialog\"\n              aria-modal=\"true\"\n              aria-label=\"Enlarged banknote\"\n              data-zoom-dialog=\"bangladesh-10-taka-2000-polimero\" hidden\n             \n             class=\"catalog-zoom-dialog\">\n              <button\n                data-zoom-close\n                aria-label=\"Close\"\n                style=\"position:absolute; top:24px; right:28px; background:transparent; border:1px solid rgba(231,222,201,0.4); color:#d8d2cd; font-size:22px; line-height:1; width:44px; height:44px; border-radius:50%; cursor:pointer;\"\n              >&times;</button>\n\n              <div style=\"position:absolute; top:24px; left:28px; display:flex; align-items:center; gap:6px; background:rgba(10,10,9,0.5); border:1px solid rgba(231,222,201,0.25); border-radius:999px; padding:6px;\">\n                <button type=\"button\" data-zoom-out\n                  disabled=\"true\"\n                  aria-label=\"Zoom out\"\n                  style=\"width:38px; height:38px; border-radius:50%; border:none; background:transparent; color:#d8d2cd; font-size:20px; cursor:pointer;\"\n                >&minus;</button>\n                <span data-zoom-percent style=\"min-width:56px; text-align:center; font-size:14px; color:#e7ddc4; letter-spacing:0.05em;\">100%</span>\n                <button\n                  disabled=\"false\"\n                  data-zoom-in aria-label=\"Zoom in\"\n                  style=\"width:38px; height:38px; border-radius:50%; border:none; background:transparent; color:#d8d2cd; font-size:20px; cursor:pointer;\"\n                >&#43;</button>\n              </div>\n\n              <div\n                style=\"overflow:hidden; max-width:100vw; max-height:100vh; width:100vw; height:100vh; touch-action:none;\"\n              >\n                <picture>\n                  <source srcset=\"/uploads/bangladesh-banco-bangladesh-10-taka-2000-polimero.webp\" type=\"image/webp\" />\n                  <img data-zoom-image\n                    src=\"/uploads/bangladesh-banco-bangladesh-10-taka-2000-polimero.jpg\"\n                    alt=\"Banknote of Diez Taka de polymer de Bangladesh Bank, enlarged view\"\n                    draggable=\"false\"\n                    style=\"display:block; max-width:100vw; max-height:100vh; width:100vw; height:100vh; object-fit:contain; transform:; cursor:zoom-in; user-select:none;\"\n                  />\n                </picture>\n              </div>\n\n              <span style=\"position:absolute; bottom:16px; left:50%; transform:translateX(-50%); font-size:14px; letter-spacing:0.06em; color:#b7ab8a; font-style:italic; pointer-events:none;\">Drag to move &middot; Mouse wheel to zoom</span>\n            </div>\n          \n        </div>\n\n        <div style=\"width:100%; max-width:760px;\">\n          \n\n          <section style=\"margin-top:44px;\">\n            <h2 style=\"font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.2em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 14px; font-style:normal;\">Historical and Issue Context</h2>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0 0 12px;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">Bangladesh's first polymer experiment:</strong>In 2000, Bangladesh Bank issued this 10 Taka note on polymer substrate as an experiment, following the path blazed by Australia in 1988 with the world's first polymer banknote.<sup style=\"font-size:12px;\">2</sup>As the Bangladesh Security Printing Corporation was only equipped for traditional paper money, the central bank commissioned this ancient issue from Note Printing Australia (NPA), a subsidiary of the Reserve Bank of Australia and a global pioneer of polymer technology.<sup style=\"font-size:12px;\">4</sup></p>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0 0 12px;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">Guardian&trade; Technology:</strong>The polymer substrate was developed in Australia by the CSIRO (national scientific body) and the Reserve Bank of Australia to combat counterfeiting, and is today marketed under the name Guardian&trade;, manufactured by CCL Secure. More than 40 central banks in the world use it in more than 175 different denominations.<sup style=\"font-size:12px;\">9</sup></p>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0 0 12px;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">A short-term experiment:</strong>Despite the polymer's durability and safety advantages, the note proved unpopular with the Bangladeshi public and was withdrawn from circulation years later, without the country permanently adopting the polymer for its paper money.<sup style=\"font-size:12px;\">2</sup></p>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">Part of the 2000&ndash;2001 banknote series:</strong>This polymer note was issued along with new paper designs of the 100 and 500 Taka denominations, within a series that incorporated for the first time the portrait of Sheikh Mujibur Rahman, father of the Bangladeshi nation, in various denominations.<sup style=\"font-size:12px;\">5</sup></p>\n          </section>\n\n          <section style=\"margin-top:36px;\">\n            <h2 style=\"font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.2em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 14px; font-style:normal;\">Key Details Visible on the Banknote</h2>\n            <ul style=\"list-style:none; margin:0; padding:0; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:14px;\">\n              <li style=\"display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:baseline;\">\n                <span style=\"width:6px; height:6px; min-width:6px; background:#5c4e33; transform:rotate(45deg); position:relative; top:-3px;\"></span>\n                <span style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.6; color:#332e22;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">Obverse:</strong>portrait of Bangabandhu Sheikh Mujibur Rahman, the Baitul Mukarram National Mosque (&ldquo;The Holy House&rdquo;) in Dhaka, and the national bird of Bangladesh, the &ldquo;doyel&rdquo; or white-backed shama (Copsychus saularis).<sup style=\"font-size:12px;\">6</sup></span>\n              </li>\n              <li style=\"display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:baseline;\">\n                <span style=\"width:6px; height:6px; min-width:6px; background:#5c4e33; transform:rotate(45deg); position:relative; top:-3px;\"></span>\n                <span style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.6; color:#332e22;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">Transparent registration:</strong>translucent window with a lotus flower, a distinctive security feature of the polymer substrate that forms a complete image when held to the light.<sup style=\"font-size:12px;\">7</sup></span>\n              </li>\n              <li style=\"display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:baseline;\">\n                <span style=\"width:6px; height:6px; min-width:6px; background:#5c4e33; transform:rotate(45deg); position:relative; top:-3px;\"></span>\n                <span style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.6; color:#332e22;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">Reverse:</strong>the National Parliament building, Jatiya Sangsad Bhaban (Sher-e-Bangla Nagar, Dhaka), designed by architect Louis Kahn, next to the National Martyrs' Memorial (Jatiyo Sriti Soudho) in Savar.<sup style=\"font-size:12px;\">8</sup></span>\n              </li>\n              <li style=\"display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:baseline;\">\n                <span style=\"width:6px; height:6px; min-width:6px; background:#5c4e33; transform:rotate(45deg); position:relative; top:-3px;\"></span>\n                <span style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.6; color:#332e22;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">Watermark:</strong>silhouette of a roaring Bengal tiger, a characteristic motif on the lower denominations of this series.<sup style=\"font-size:12px;\">2</sup></span>\n              </li>\n              <li style=\"display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:baseline;\">\n                <span style=\"width:6px; height:6px; min-width:6px; background:#5c4e33; transform:rotate(45deg); position:relative; top:-3px;\"></span>\n                <span style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.6; color:#332e22;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">Security thread:</strong>Simulated solid thread with text in Bengali, embedded in the plastic substrate.<sup style=\"font-size:12px;\">2</sup></span>\n              </li>\n              <li style=\"display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:baseline;\">\n                <span style=\"width:6px; height:6px; min-width:6px; background:#5c4e33; transform:rotate(45deg); position:relative; top:-3px;\"></span>\n                <span style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.6; color:#332e22;\"><strong style=\"color:#1c1a15;\">Color:</strong>Printing predominantly in red and pink tones, with bilingual texts in Bengali and English and serial numbering in both languages.</span>\n              </li>\n            </ul>\n          </section>\n\n          <section style=\"margin-top:36px;\">\n            <h2 style=\"font-size:15px; letter-spacing:0.2em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 14px; font-style:normal;\">Additional Context</h2>\n            <p style=\"font-size:19px; line-height:1.65; color:#332e22; margin:0;\">The 10 Taka note in permanent circulation has existed in Bangladesh since 1972, with multiple redesigns since then.<sup style=\"font-size:12px;\">1</sup>This polymer issue from 2000 represents a distinct and ephemeral branch of that history &mdash;a chapter shared with more than three dozen countries that have experimented with the plastic substrate since Australia first introduced it in 1988, as documented in this collection's World Polymer Banknote catalogue.</p>\n          </section>\n\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div style=\"width:100%; max-width:760px; margin:44px auto 0; padding-top:20px; border-top:1px solid rgba(10,10,9,0.12);\">\n        <h2 style=\"font-size:13px; letter-spacing:0.14em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5c4e33; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 10px; font-style:normal;\">Notes</h2>\n        <p style=\"font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; color:#5c4e33; margin:0 0 6px;\">1. Wikipedia. &ldquo;Bangladeshi 10-taka note.&rdquo;<em>en.wikipedia.org</em>.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; color:#5c4e33; margin:0 0 6px;\">2. Wikipedia. &ldquo;Banknotes of the Bangladeshi taka.&rdquo;<em>en.wikipedia.org</em>: 10 Taka polymer note issued between 2000&ndash;2001, then withdrawn due to low popularity.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; color:#5c4e33; margin:0 0 6px;\">3. ATSnotes. &ldquo;Bangladesh banknotes &mdash; Bangladesh paper money catalog.&rdquo;<em>atsnotes.com/catalog/banknotes/bangladesh.html</em>: rank Pick 35&ndash;38 (2000&ndash;01), 10 Taka as the first denomination of the group.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; color:#5c4e33; margin:0 0 6px;\">4. eBay listing and cataloging of collectors, note identified as Pick P-35, printed by Note Printing Australia.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; color:#5c4e33; margin:0 0 6px;\">5. Wikipedia. &ldquo;Banknotes of the Bangladeshi taka&rdquo;: series printed between 2000 and 2001, with new designs on 100 and 500 Taka paper and the incorporation of the portrait of Sheikh Mujibur Rahman.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; color:#5c4e33; margin:0 0 6px;\">6. LA Currency. &ldquo;BDT &mdash; Bangladesh Taka.&rdquo;<em>lacurrency.com/bdt-bangladeshi-taka</em>: national emblem, Baitul Mukarram mosque and doyel bird on the obverse of the lower denominations of this series.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; color:#5c4e33; margin:0 0 6px;\">7. Numista. &ldquo;10 Taka &mdash; Bangladesh&rdquo;, note #204760.<em>en.numista.com</em>: transparent register with floral motif, safety feature of the polymer substrate.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; color:#5c4e33; margin:0 0 6px;\">8. Numist, note #204760: identification of the National Parliament building (Jatiya Sangsad Bhaban) and the National Monument to the Martyrs on the reverse.</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; color:#5c4e33; margin:0;\">9. CCL Secure. Corporate information on the Guardian&trade; polymer substrate technology, originally developed by CSIRO and the Reserve Bank of Australia.</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </main>\n\n  \n\n</div>",
      "recordTitle": "Bangladesh Bank",
      "eyebrow": "World Polymer Banknotes · Bangladesh · 2000"
    }
  }
